ready1_open_rewrite.raw_answer_text:
\textbf{Solution:} The coordinates of point $D$ are $(3,3)$; the coordinates of point $E$ are $(1,0)$;\\
Let the equation of line $EF$ be $y=kx+b$,\\
therefore $\left\{\begin{array}{l}
k+b=0 \\
3k+b=\frac{3}{2}
\end{array}\right.$,\\
thus, $\left\{\begin{array}{l}
k=\frac{3}{4} \\
b=-\frac{3}{4}
\end{array}\right.$,\\
hence the equation of line $EF$ is $\boxed{y=\frac{3}{4}x-\frac{3}{4}}$;

